en.fuller:
κατ-αρτίζω
[in LXX chiefly in Ps (Psa.8:2 al.; כּוּן, etc.) and Ezra (כְּלַל) ;]
to render ἄρτιος, i.e. fit, complete;
__(a) to mend, repair: Mat.4:21, Mrk.1:19;
__(b) to furnish completely, complete, equip, prepare: pass., Luk.6:40, Rom.9:22, Heb.11:3; mid., Mat.21:16 (LXX), Heb.10:5 (LXX);
__(with) in ethical sense, to prepare, complete, perfect: Gal.6:1 (EV, restore), 1Pe.5:10; pass., 1Co.1:10 (Field, Notes, 167), 2Co.13:11, Heb.13:21 (cf. προ-καταρτίζω).†
(AS)

es.fuller:
κατ-αρτίζω
[en LXX princ. in Ps (Sal.8:2 etc.; כּוּן, etc.) and Ezra (כְּלַל) ;]
to render ἄρτιος, es decir fit, complete;
(a) to mend, repair: Mt.4:21, Mc.1:19;
(b) to furnish completely, complete, equip, prepare: pas., Lc.6:40, Ro.9:22, Heb.11:3; med., Mt.21:16 (LXX), Heb.10:5 (LXX);
(with) in ethical sense, to prepare, complete, perfect: Gá.6:1 (EV, restore), 1P.5:10; pas., 1Co.1:10 (Field, Notes, 167), 2Co.13:11, Heb.13:21 (cf. προ-καταρτίζω).†
(AS)

he.fuller:
κατ-αρτίζω
[בשבעים בעיקר in Ps (תה.8:2 ועוד; כּוּן, ועוד) and Ezra (כְּלַל) ;]
to render ἄρτιος, כלומר fit, complete;
(a) to mend, repair: מתי.4:21, מרקוס.1:19;
(b) to furnish completely, complete, equip, prepare: סביל, לוקס.6:40, רומים.9:22, עב.11:3; בינוני, מתי.21:16 (LXX), עב.10:5 (LXX);
(with) in ethical sense, to prepare, complete, perfect: גל.6:1 (EV, restore), 1פ.5:10; סביל, 1קור.1:10 (Field, Notes, 167), 2קור.13:11, עב.13:21 (השוו προ-καταρτίζω).†
(AS)
